@defgroup micro-os-plus-micro-test-plus µTest++
@brief The µTest++ Testing Framework.

@details
µTest++ is a C++20 testing framework for embedded targets, which also runs
on the native platforms. The tests are ordinary C++ code, functions and
lambdas, with no preprocessor macros.

A test program uses three classes:
- the `runner`, which reads the command line, runs the suites, and
  returns the exit code;
- the `suite`, a named group of test cases;
- the `test_case`, a named sequence of checks, made with `expect()` and
  `require()`.

The results are written in the TAP format, for the tools that read test
results, or in a human-readable format.

The topics are grouped in four parts:
- how to write the tests, in @ref micro-os-plus-micro-test-plus-cpp-api;
- how to test C code, in @ref micro-os-plus-micro-test-plus-c-api;
- the macros that enable the framework, in
  @ref micro-os-plus-micro-test-plus-config;
- the options of the test programs, in
  @ref micro-os-plus-micro-test-plus-cli.
